Sudan's paramilitary Rapid Support Forces (RSF) committed crimes against humanity and ethnic cleansing while deliberately targeting children during their campaign to seize El Fasher, the capital of North Darfur state, Amnesty International said on Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cebe6a40-7532-11f1-b380-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25341684040183.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cebe6a40-7532-11f1-b380-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25341684040183.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e249049a-7531-11f1-b895-ad9b86483aa0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 10:29:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cebe6a40-7532-11f1-b380-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25341684040183.jpg">AP - Marwan Ali</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Thousands rush to get tickets for Bayeux Tapestry's UK show</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260701-thousands-rush-to-get-tickets-for-bayeux-tapestry-s-uk-show</link><description>
Thousands rushed to get tickets Wednesday for the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition in London, with the 11th-century artwork depicting the 1066 Norman conquest of England set to be transported from France for its first showing in the UK.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ed4f882-7535-11f1-bedb-c774f26789d8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 10:14:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/09a31122-5faa-11f1-8f11-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/4854842b2950ba8ef1c9b01c8b5129e96b7395e2.jpg">© Lou BENOIST / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Mali's shifting alliances fuel a deepening cycle of civilian suffering, HWR says</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260701-human-rights-watch-reports-grave-abuses-from-all-sides-in-mali-since-april-attacks</link><description>
Human Rights Watch (HWR) says the army, allied militias and Islamist armed groups have all committed abuses with impunity since the attacks in northern Mali in April, and its latest report highlights a pattern of impunity that demands urgent action.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a91e28b0-4243-11f1-b76f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A92J2CE-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a91e28b0-4243-11f1-b76f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A92J2CE-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2bd846e-73a6-11f1-8bc3-cb75072d777a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 12:58:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a91e28b0-4243-11f1-b76f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A92J2CE-1.jpg">AFP - ABDOLLAH AG MOHAMED</source><dc:creator>Melissa Chemam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>South Africa protesters confront migrant homes during nationwide marches</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260701-south-africa-protesters-confront-migrant-homes-during-nationwide-marches</link><description>
Protesters stopped outside buildings believed to house undocumented migrants and urged residents to leave as thousands marched across South Africa on Tuesday, the deadline set by anti-immigration groups for foreigners without papers to leave the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8d8d5f6-74b1-11f1-992f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T165841Z-969527858-RC2C4MA8UPF8-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8d8d5f6-74b1-11f1-992f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T165841Z-969527858-RC2C4MA8UPF8-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">461c0fbe-7526-11f1-8b2d-7129b96364f7</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 08:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c8d8d5f6-74b1-11f1-992f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T165841Z-969527858-RC2C4MA8UPF8-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg">© Rogan Ward / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>World's oceans record hottest June ever as new El Nino takes hold</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260701-world-s-oceans-record-hottest-june-ever-as-new-el-nino-takes-hold</link><description>
The world's oceans reached their hottest June on record, scientists said on Wednesday, with sea temperatures expected to climb further as El Nino develops alongside human-driven climate change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/475bfbf0-386a-11ea-a7a7-005056bfd1d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2017071818175613711.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/475bfbf0-386a-11ea-a7a7-005056bfd1d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2017071818175613711.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd3ca334-751e-11f1-8dac-1bff2aa3277d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 07:31:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/475bfbf0-386a-11ea-a7a7-005056bfd1d9/w:1024/p:16x9/2017071818175613711.jpg">Flickr / Creative Commons</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ireland takes over EU presidency with French naval help on security</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260701-ireland-takes-over-eu-presidency-with-french-naval-help-on-security</link><description>
Ireland takes over the rotating presidency of the Council of the European Union on Wednesday with French and British military assets expected to help protect a six-month programme of high-level meetings, as Dublin prepares for what security officials describe as an unusually demanding operation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21297916-745f-11f1-83a2-c9a0ace6ef83</guid><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 06:09:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/36cabbfe-7478-11f1-bfb3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-33GL4GB.jpg">AFP - RICHARD A. BROOKS</source><dc:creator>David Coffey</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French justice system to re-examine 88,000 child abuse claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260630-french-justice-system-to-re-examine-88-000-child-abuse-claims</link><description>
Some 88,000 complaints regarding sexual violence against children are being re-examined by investigative services – a figure higher than the 70,000 initially ordered by Justice Minister Gérald Darmanin last month. This comes in the wake of the murder of 11-year-old Lyhanna, whose death prompted public outrage over the state's mishandling of child abuse cases.
